# RBS's core signature of Data leaves out that its classes are built and initialized with their members as keywords,
# so a Data class's new could not be called with them, nor super from an initialize that freezes or checks them. This
# declares what Ruby does; each class's own initialize signature names the members.
class Data
  def self.new: (**untyped) -> instance
              | ...

  def initialize: (**untyped) -> void
end
